stateDiagram-v2
    %% Per-network IRC connection lifecycle, owned by irc.Manager.runNetwork.
    %% The three persisted/published states are irc.NetworkState values;
    %% the rest are internal steps of one connect attempt.

    [*] --> Stopped : network row exists, no runtime

    Stopped --> Connecting : StartNetwork (boot from config.yaml,<br/>POST /api/networks/{id}/connect)

    state Connecting {
        [*] --> RefreshCommands : runNetwork iteration begins
        RefreshCommands --> Dialing : ListNetworkConnectCommands(networkID)
        Dialing --> TLS12Fallback : dial error and TLS downgrade possible
        TLS12Fallback --> Dialing : one retry, TLSMaxVersion = TLS 1.2
        Dialing --> Registering : TCP + TLS handshake ok
        Registering --> Authenticating : CAP LS, NICK, USER, optional PASS
        Authenticating --> [*] : 001 RPL_WELCOME<br/>(or SASL 903 first)
    }

    Connecting --> Connected : RPL_WELCOME<br/>publish NetworkStateEvent{connected}
    Connecting --> Disconnected : dial or registration failed<br/>markDisconnected

    state Connected {
        [*] --> Joining : run connect commands
        Joining --> Synced : JOIN + NAMES + TOPIC per channel
        Synced --> Backfilling : server advertises CHATHISTORY
        Backfilling --> Synced : BATCH inserted,<br/>publish HistoryBackfillEvent
        Synced --> Synced : PRIVMSG / presence / mode traffic
    }

    Connected --> Disconnected : socket closed, ERROR, QUIT,<br/>or ctx cancel -> markDisconnected

    Disconnected --> Backoff : ctx still alive
    Backoff --> Connecting : after backoff,<br/>server index rotates to the next entry

    note right of Backoff
        Backoff starts at 1s, doubles per attempt,
        caps at 5 minutes. It is never reset on a
        successful connect, so a network that
        flaps repeatedly keeps the long delay.
    end note

    note right of Disconnected
        markDisconnected compares the runtime
        generation: if a newer runtime already owns
        this network (StopNetwork then restart) it
        returns without touching conn/state and
        without publishing, so the live connection
        is never contradicted.
    end note

    Connected --> Stopped : StopNetwork (DELETE/PATCH network,<br/>POST .../disconnect, shutdown)
    Connecting --> Stopped : StopNetwork
    Backoff --> Stopped : StopNetwork or baseCtx cancelled
    Stopped --> [*]
